<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net6.0;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Version>1.10.51</Version>
		<Authors>Sergi Ortiz Gomez</Authors>
		<Company>DrUalcman</Company>
		<Description>Manage IndexedDb from Blazor WebAssembly applications. Create a StoreDbContext similar how is working in EF. Please report any bug or changes you need using our contact form in the web site. Thanks.</Description>
		<Copyright>Free</Copyright>
		<PackageLicenseFile>License.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageTags>webassembly, blazor, indexedDb, interop, javascript, database</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
			1.10.51 — offline writes never wrote anything, and updating a missing row took the batch down.

			- AddAsync(row, isOffline: true) and UpdateAsync(row, isOffline: true) always failed with
			"[Insert] StoreName can't be null" and never touched the database. The offline write adds
			an OffLine flag to each row by turning it into an ExpandoObject, then handed the result
			back to the ordinary insert — where TModel is no longer your entity but object. Resolving
			the store from it asked for one belonging to a model named "Object", got null, and the
			guard against a null store name refused the call. Nothing was ever wrong with the
			database, so deleting and recreating it made no difference. The store name is now
			resolved once from the caller's TModel and passed down as a parameter. If you use the
			offline flag, this is the release that makes it work at all.
			- DbInsert and DbUpdate gained an overload taking the store name explicitly. The existing
			signatures resolve it and delegate, so no caller changes.
			- Update on a row that does not exist no longer aborts the whole transaction. It read the
			stored row first to keep the columns the caller left out, and from undefined that merge
			produced an empty object: put({}) then threw DataError because the key path yields no
			value, and it threw from inside the request handler where the surrounding try cannot see
			it — which in IndexedDB rolls back every other row in the batch. put is an upsert, so a
			row that is not there yet now goes in as-is, the handler body is wrapped, and a rejected
			row calls preventDefault() so the failure stays that row's. Updating a row another part
			of the app had just deleted was enough to reach this.
</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/drualcman/BlasorIndexedDb</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>Git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageId>DrUalcman-BlazorIndexedDb</PackageId>
		<Product>BlazorIndexedDb</Product>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://blazorindexdb.community-mall.com/</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<AssemblyName>DrUalcman-BlazorIndexedDb</AssemblyName>
		<RootNamespace>BlazorIndexedDb</RootNamespace>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<AnalysisLevel>6.0</AnalysisLevel>
		<EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>True</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
		<ErrorReport>send</ErrorReport>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<Nullable>disable</Nullable>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
		<DocumentationFile>C:\DrUalcman\BlasorIndexedDb\BlasorIndexedDb\BlazorIndexedDb.xml</DocumentationFile>
		<GenerateSerializationAssemblies>Auto</GenerateSerializationAssemblies>
	</PropertyGroup>


	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="6.0.36" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net6.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="8.0.29" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="9.0.18" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web" Version="10.0.10" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="6.0.36" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net6.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="8.0.29" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="9.0.18" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly" Version="10.0.10" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="License.txt">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath></PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
